s/vercel/next.js/issues/40368","id":1241298837,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBC3Cis5J_LeV","user":{"login":"rubytree33","id":110690041,"node_id":"U_kgDOBpj--Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110690041?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33","html_url":"https://github.com/rubytree33","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-08T22:26:49Z","updated_at":"2022-09-08T22:39:08Z","body":"As a disclaimer I'm not a maintainer and I'm very new here.\r\n\r\nThe reproduction does have the warning. For those looking for it, [here](https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/import-esm-externals) is the relevant part of the docs for an error this option is meant to circumvent. It says the option \"tries to automatically correct this error\" but all I can find for its actual use (according to the comments) is to enable a short procedure after [this check](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/f7eed07945375f0b4a76efcbb5cbfe87072c2261/packages/next/build/webpack-config.ts#L455-L459). I'm still trying to figure out what this actually does in the code.\r\n\r\nIf it does need to change, I think [this](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/f7eed07945375f0b4a76efcbb5cbfe87072c2261/packages/next/server/config-schema.ts#L241-L243) is the part of the schema that this type requirement comes from, and I'll just make a pull request that changes it.\r\n\r\n(By the way, the relevant documentation isn't linked with the warning, and I couldn't find any other documentation for this option. Maybe it would be good to have documentation links to configuration warnings like this? I might open a new issue for that.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/1241298837/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rubytree33","id":110690041,"node_id":"U_kgDOBpj--Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110690041?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33","html_url":"https://github.com/rubytree33","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"actor":{"login":"rubytree33","id":110690041,"node_id":"U_kgDOBpj--Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110690041?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33","html_url":"https://github.com/rubytree33","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.g