e_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/deployments","created_at":"2016-10-05T23:32:51Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T14:51:52Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T14:29:08Z","git_url":"git://github.com/vercel/next.js.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:vercel/next.js.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js","homepage":"https://nextjs.org","size":2429859,"stargazers_count":136480,"watchers_count":136480,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":30029,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3156,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["blog","browser","compiler","components","hybrid","nextjs","node","react","server-rendering","ssg","static","static-site-generator","universal","vercel"],"visibility":"public","forks":30029,"open_issues":3156,"watchers":136480,"default_branch":"canary","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Describe the feature you'd like to request\n\nThe warning issued in the reproduction for #40368 does not link to documentation for the relevant option, which is [here](https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/import-esm-externals), and instead only links general documentation for an invalid config ([here](https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/invalid-next-config)) which itself only links general documentation for `next.config.js` ([here](https://nextjs.org/docs/api-reference/next.config.js/introduction)), which at the bottom links to a [file](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/canary/packages/next/server/config-shared.ts) which only describes (in code) what some of the configuration options do, besides their types.\r\n\r\nAlmost none of the experimental configuration options are described, which maybe isn't as surprising because they are likely to change but it is still difficult to tell what they are for from looking at this.\r\n\r\n(While the linked issue may not be giving a warning correctly, this happens for `next.config.js` warnings in general. The link to documentation should directly, or almost directly, explain why the configuration in the warning is not the right type.)\r\n\r\nIn code, the warnings apparently come from [here](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/614f0d8e19a80cbb5f707b2201c7fb3ec5f3a831/packages/next/server/config.ts#L787-L801).\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like\n\nIdeally, rewrite the warning code to link in the warning directly to documentation for the relevant configuration option(s). I'm not sure if such documentation pages exist, so they might also need to be written.\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered\n\nAdd a link to the [useful links](https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/invalid-next-config#useful-links) of the page that is already linked to documentation for all the configuration options, ideally a list that can be easily searched. I'm also not sure this page exists.\r\n\r\nThe simplest option is to just link to [this file](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/canary/packages/next/server/config-shared.ts), though it might need a little more explanation about what it is since it isn't a documentation page on its own. It might be helpful to add more comments to it on what the options do if it's effectively the documentation for the list of configuration options.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/40375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/40375/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/1241352405","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/40368#issuecomment-1241352405","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/40368","id":1241352405,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBC3Cis5J_YjV","user":{"login":"rubytree33","id":110690041,"node_id":"U_kgDOBpj--Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110690041?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33","html_url":"https://github.com/rubytree33","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubytree33/repos","events_url":"https://api.githu